/**
 * @page topic_client_main Client Lifecycle
 * @ingroup module_client
 * @brief Client startup, session orchestration, reconnect, and teardown.
 *
 * The client entry point assembles options, platform/media subsystems, the
 * presentation layer, and one shared network connection. It coordinates these
 * owners; packet framing and backend I/O belong to the network runtime.
 *
 * @section client_main_start Startup
 *
 * Startup parses options, initializes logging and platform services, prepares
 * capture/audio as requested, starts terminal presentation when interactive,
 * and establishes the endpoint. `network_connection_establish()` performs
 * backend selection and ACIP negotiation before producers publish.
 *
 * @section client_main_running Running session
 *
 * Capture, audio, keepalive, and UI producers run independently. They publish
 * through subsystem APIs and the connection's `acip_transport_t`; they do not
 * coordinate by sharing a raw socket. The TUI consumes snapshots separately.
 *
 * @section client_main_reconnect Reconnect
 *
 * A recoverable transport loss stops producers, drains the old connection, and
 * creates a new connection with fresh transport and security state. Fatal
 * configuration, authentication, protocol, or cancellation errors exit instead
 * of being silently retried.
 *
 * @section client_main_shutdown Shutdown
 *
 * SIGINT only requests exit. The owner stops producers, joins workers, retires
 * live TUI screens, restores the terminal, destroys the connection, and releases
 * media/platform resources in dependency order.
 *
 * @see topic_client_connection
 * @see topic_tui
 * @see topic_network
 */
